  // ── FAQs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  faqs: [
    { q: 'What Cambridge examination centres serve Türkiye?',                                                                        a: 'British Council Istanbul is the primary Cambridge IGCSE and A-Level examination centre in Türkiye. British Council Ankara serves the capital. From summer 2026 British Embassy School Ankara (BESA) operates as authorised Cambridge International iGCSE examination centre in British Embassy grounds. Izmir, Antalya, Bursa, and Adana families travel to Istanbul or Ankara for examinations (short domestic flight or drive). Private candidate fees run approximately £80-120 per subject; a full 8-subject IGCSE sitting costs approximately £640-960.' },
    { q: 'How does the TRT time zone work with Nairobi teaching hours?',                                                            a: 'Türkiye Time (TRT UTC+3) is exactly East Africa Time (EAT UTC+3) — zero offset. Smartious live classes 9 AM – 12 PM local time in Istanbul, Ankara, Izmir, Antalya, Bursa, and Adana run simultaneously with 9 AM – 12 PM Nairobi teaching hours. This is the only Smartious market outside East Africa itself with zero scheduling friction. Afternoon 2 PM – 5 PM slot also available. Recorded sessions 24/7.' },
    { q: 'What Turkish universities accept Cambridge, IB, and AP qualifications?',                                                   a: 'All major Turkish universities — Boğaziçi University (Istanbul, English-medium public), METU/ODTÜ (Ankara, English-medium public research), Istanbul Technical University (ITU), Koç University (private, Istanbul, English-medium), Sabancı University (private, Tuzla near Istanbul, English-medium), Bilkent University (Ankara), Bahçeşehir University (Istanbul, English-medium private), Türk-Alman Üniversitesi (Turkish-German bilingual). Foundation-to-degree entry via Cambridge A-Level or IB Diploma is streamlined; Turkish citizen students may parallel-prepare for YKS national exam.' },
    { q: 'How does Smartious pricing work with Turkish lira volatility?',                                                            a: 'Smartious USD-only pricing (Online tier USD 180/month ≈ TRY 6,300/month, Online Plus USD 300/month ≈ TRY 10,500/month, Premium USD 540/month ≈ TRY 19,000/month at current rates). Full year USD 2,160-6,480 = TRY 76,000-227,000. Predictable annual USD budget without TRY inflation exposure — specifically valuable for Turkish and expat families whose salaries are TRY-denominated but international school fees may be USD-quoted at premium schools.' },
    { q: 'Can Iranian diaspora families in Istanbul use Smartious?',                                                                 a: 'Yes — this is one of Smartious\'s specific value propositions for Türkiye. Istanbul hosts the largest Iranian expatriate concentration outside Iran (approximately 2-3 million Iranians in Türkiye, largest urban concentration in Şişli, Beyoğlu, Beşiktaş, Nişantaşı). Iranian families in Türkiye pay via Turkish banking or USD wire, access Cambridge / IB / OSSD without the sanctions constraints on Iran itself, and use international qualifications for university applications globally.' },
    { q: 'We\'re a Russian or Ukrainian family relocated post-2022. How does Smartious help?',                                       a: 'Common Türkiye family situation since February 2022 across Istanbul (Levent, Sarıyer, Beyoğlu, Ataşehir) and Antalya (Konyaaltı, Lara). Smartious delivers English-medium Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, IB Diploma, American AP, or Ontario OSSD — university pathway options independent of Russian or Ukrainian national curriculum politics. Cambridge and IB accepted at UK Russell Group, EU universities, Australian Group of Eight, Canadian U15, US Ivy League.' },
    { q: 'How does Ontario OSSD work for Turkish families targeting Canada?',                                                       a: 'Via our Canadian Cross International School (CCIS) partnership. Only Keystone International Schools (Küçük Çamlıca + Çekmeköy Istanbul) offers Ontario curriculum physically in Türkiye. Smartious extends OSSD access to all Turkish cities online. Turkish families targeting Toronto, McGill, UBC, McMaster, Waterloo, Western, Queen\'s apply via OUAC as Ontario secondary graduates.' },
    { q: 'Can Turkish citizen children combine MEB (Turkish national) school with Smartious for Cambridge?',                        a: 'Yes — a common Turkish family configuration. MEB Turkish national school in the morning, Smartious Cambridge / IB / AP in the afternoon (2 PM – 5 PM TRT window). Family combines Turkish qualifications (LGS transition exam, YKS national exam) with international qualifications (Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level) for maximum university options — Turkish universities via YKS + international destinations via Cambridge / IB.' },
    { q: 'What Turkish cities does Smartious serve?',                                                                                a: 'Istanbul (Bebek, Etiler, Nişantaşı, Şişli, Zekeriyaköy, Ortaköy, Kadıköy, Ataşehir, Üsküdar), Ankara (Çankaya, Bilkent, Oran, GOP), Izmir (Alsancak, Karşıyaka, Bornova, Çeşme coast), Antalya (Konyaaltı, Lara, Muratpaşa, Belek — post-2022 Russian and Ukrainian community), Bursa (Nilüfer — automotive corporate families), and Adana (southern Türkiye — underserved market). Also broader Aegean coast, Mediterranean coast, and eastern Türkiye via live online delivery.' },
    { q: 'What internet speed does Smartious require in Türkiye?',                                                                 a: 'Sustained ~5-10 Mbps per student for live HD video conferencing. Türk Telekom Fiber, Vodafone Turkey Fiber, and Turkcell Superonline residential broadband across Istanbul, Ankara, Izmir, and other Turkish cities routinely deliver 100+ Mbps. 5G mobile widely available in major cities.' },
  ],

